If you have multiple metrics and/or multiple treatments and are running hypothesis tests, then there is an increased chance of finding a false positive. To correct for this we do the Bonferroni correction and multiply the p-value by the number of metrics in a tier times the number of treatments. Click to learn more.

Uncorrected significance: {uncorrectedSignificance}
Corrected significance: {significance}

experimentTable.cupedCorrectionTooltip:
