      confidenceInterval {The range of absolute performance values likely to occur on rollout. The level of confidence is set in the "Statistical Settings" dropdown and defaults to 95%.}
      relativeChange {The relative difference between each test variant and control.}
      significance {The likelihood that the performance displayed for each test variant is actually nonzero and not due to random fluctuations in the data. The higher this number, the more confident we are of the result. Equivalent to 100 * (1-p value).}
